  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "16. Actions",
    "ruleNumber": "16.01",
    "summary": "Each Action states when it starts, which friendly units may perform it, its use limit, when it completes, its effect and any extra restrictions. A unit cannot **start an Action** if it:\n\n- is off the battlefield\n- is **AIRCRAFT** or **FORTIFICATION**\n- is **[Battle-shocked](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock)**\n- has an [Objective Control](vsdata:core-rule/profiles) value of 0 or –\n- is **[Engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range)**, other than a **TITANIC** unit\n- [Advanced](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) or [Fell Back](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back) this turn\n- already started an Action this turn\n\nOnce it starts one, until the turn ends it cannot declare a charge, and it can shoot only if it is **TITANIC**.\n\nIt fails to complete the Action if it leaves the battlefield or makes any move other than a [Pile-in](vsdata:core-rule/pile-in-move) or [Consolidation](vsdata:core-rule/consolidation-move); otherwise the Action's Effect applies when it completes.",
